  "worked_solution": "The unit price of candy is $$2.15/lb.$ To find the cost of $3$ pounds of candy, we multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2.15\\times 3 & =6.45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Lisa would pay $$6.45$ for $3$ pounds of candy.",
